{"path":"docs/equations-steps.md","title":"Equations: the model step by step","html":"<!-- math -->\n<h1>Equations: the model step by step</h1>\n<p><em>Model version 6 (<a href=\"#/doc/docs/model-versions.md\">what changed in each version</a>).</em></p>\n<p>The model is built up one mechanism at a time, so each step&#39;s effect can be seen on its own. Step 1 is the <a href=\"#/doc/docs/equations-simple.md\">simple model</a>. Step 5 has exactly the <a href=\"#/doc/docs/equations.md\">full model</a>&#39;s mechanisms and agents; the full model then compares six sharing rules (imposed or chosen, with or without flow-back) where step 5 sweeps α with agents choosing. The full model&#39;s optional extras (costly or wrong sharing, learning from failure) stay off in both. Every step uses the same idea graph, bounties and knowledge reward: a published idea earns 1 per new bit, flowing back with <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Step</th>\n<th>Adds</th>\n<th>Equations</th>\n<th>Setting</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td><strong>The simple model: identical agents, α and β set.</strong> 12 identical agents, equal money each round. <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0528em;\">β</span></span></span></span> are set.</td>\n<td><a href=\"#/doc/docs/equations-simple.md\">simple model</a></td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td><strong>Agents choose what to share, so β comes out of their choices.</strong> Each agent publishes an idea when its reward beats the risk a rival uses it to win a bounty first. <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0528em;\">β</span></span></span></span> is no longer set: it comes out of the choices.</td>\n<td><a href=\"#/doc/docs/equations.md?at=9-choosing-whether-to-share-where-%CE%B2-comes-from\">section 9</a></td>\n<td>visibility: choice</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td><strong>Half the money follows earnings.</strong> Half of each round&#39;s money goes to agents by what they earned.</td>\n<td><a href=\"#/doc/docs/equations.md?at=5-money-each-round\">section 5</a></td>\n<td><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.5</span></span></span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td><strong>Different kinds of agents.</strong> 3 foundation builders, 3 target racers, 2 cheap explorers, 2 specialists, a free rider and 1 plain agent.</td>\n<td><a href=\"#/doc/docs/equations.md?at=8-choosing-what-to-attempt\">section 8</a></td>\n<td>the agent mix</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td><strong>Adds a gamer and validation; same as the full model.</strong> The last plain agent becomes a gamer, who spends some attempts on trivial ideas; validators reject them half the time. A trivial idea adds no new bits, so it earns nothing.</td>\n<td><a href=\"#/doc/docs/equations.md?at=6-the-mint\">section 6</a></td>\n<td>gamer 1, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.5</span></span></span></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><strong>What is compared.</strong> At step 1, societies by <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0528em;\">β</span></span></span></span>. From step 2, <strong>traditional</strong> (finished work only, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>) against <strong>agents choosing</strong> at several <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span></span></span></span>, since <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0528em;\">β</span></span></span></span> is now their choice. The <strong>sharing</strong> measure shows the <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0528em;\">β</span></span></span></span> that came out.</p>\n<p><strong>Reading the steps.</strong> If a mechanism matters, the gap between traditional and OSO changes at the step that adds it. Step 2 is the key one for OSO&#39;s claim: it shows whether flow-back (<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.5782em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0037em;\">α</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">&lt;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>) makes agents choose to share.</p>\n"}